# middle-edge case with stops tried at the 180-degree vertices: two holes 1 mm off wall v=0 end exactly at u=300 and u=700;
# primary at-face e1 through 500 -> a hole face cannot cover the full width of a wall-flush timber (holes never touch the outer ring, I2) -> no stop (R6)
surface 1 origin 0 0 2500 u +x v +y outline 0,0 300,0 700,0 1000,0 1000,1000 0,1000 hole 200,1 300,1 300,100 200,100 hole 700,1 800,1 800,100 700,100
timber 1 27 33 role boundary
timber 2 27 33 role boundary
timber 3 27 33 role primary
place 1 on 1 at-face e5 -v +n
place 2 on 1 at-face e3 +v +n
place 3 on 1 at-face e1 through 500 +u +n
